      "message": "Put a card on the door and a guide on the empty repository\n\nSigning in, asking for a reset and choosing a new password are one\ncard on a quiet page: the mark, the title, the fields, the button, the\nother ways in under a rule. The field is labelled Username. Signing up\nis the same card. New repository is a panel of fields. The first-run\npage is the same rows as everywhere else.\n\nA repository's page opens with its name, its description, and chips for\nits visibility, branch, latest tag and tip, with Clone behind a control\nthat shows the address and copies it. An empty repository shows the\nthree ways to put something on the anvil as a segmented control over\none code frame: push a change, import history, or let an agent start.\nIts files are rows in a panel; its rail is a stack of panels: the rules\nthe branch lands under as the sentences the change page uses, the open\nchanges, the landing queue, who is at work here, and tags.\n\nRepository settings is one page with a sub-navigation and a panel per\ndecision: visibility as a segment, ownership, the landing policy as\nfields and checks with its preview and simulation as panels, the mirror\nfor the operator, description, name, archive and delete.\n\nChange-Id: Iwork0130c\nTask: t-5b9sy6ehtkrrm0h62s6btdtmnf\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
